  "question": {
    "text": "A hemispherical vessel is completely filled with a liquid of refractive index $\\mu$. A small coin is kept at the lowest point $(\\mathrm{O})$ of the vessel as shown in figure. The minimum value of the refractive index of the liquid so that a person can see the coin from point E (at the level of the vessel) is\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4cutAfDv9ZzhFu9iHam4ktN5KyMXf2SE4YOVeXH31OE.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "inBM8",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Mc4cK",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZKqNd",
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "F3KDv",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/i2Lhq4wB3sWeKzZHN0GsQi3nWZNwtCLUbpJImKnIlUw.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nFor the rays from coin to reach the point $E$, the refracted rays must grazing the surface, i.e. they must be incident at critical angle $\\theta_c$ inside the liquid.\n$\\mu=\\frac{1}{\\sin \\theta_c}$\n$\\mu$ is minimum when $\\theta_c$ is maximum.\nMaximum value of $\\theta_c=45^{\\circ}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\mu$ has a minimum value of $\\sqrt{2}$.",
    "image": null
  },
